core_incr_roic":100.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":-0.07701960183192692,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":7.7,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":0.023149050959786165,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":73.1,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.06071869613585915,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":78.6,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.05604254669028536,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":6.6,"_gate_insider_own":0.0871,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":58.1,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"DraftKings Inc. operates as a digital sports entertainment and gaming company in the United States and internationally. The company offers online and retail sports betting, daily fantasy sports, digital lottery couriers, prediction markets, and other products, as well as retails sportsbooks. It also provides iGaming, or online casino products, which includes blackjack, roulette, baccarat and slot machines. In addition, the company engages in the design and development of sports betting and casino gaming software for online and retail sportsbooks, and iGaming operators. DraftKings Inc. was founded in 2011 and is headquartered in Boston, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jason D. Robins | Co-Founder, Chairman & CEO | Age 44 | Compensation: $3.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 5K people. Revenue per employee of $1.1M ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, with revenue growing 39%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $118K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $62K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (9/10).","financial_summary":["DraftKings Inc. is a mid-cap consumer cyclical business with a $9.4B market cap on $6.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +39% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +22.4pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at -5444% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The business throws off $648M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 11 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 178.67\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin -0.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 6.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 8.7% of the shares, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.8) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 8.8% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant goodwill (35% of assets) from past acquisitions \u2014 a soft asset a conservative appraisal discounts to zero","sev":"amber","cat":"balance_sheet"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Shares offer a 20% margin of safety against estimated fair value","Trading near the bottom of its 52-week range \u2014 the market is offering a discount","Valued at a 1251% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Insiders are net buyers (67% buy ratio) \u2014 insiders sell for many reasons but buy for only one","Growing faster than most Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Among the least levered in Consumer Cyclical \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"DraftKings (DKNG) Securities Investigation Notice - Levi & Korsinsky","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/draftkings-dkng-securities-investigation-notice---levi--korsinsky-302939116.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794597000.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["legal"]},{"title":"Here\u2019s Why Wells Fargo Downgraded DraftKings (DKNG)","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link